               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="10XX/11XX">s. xi/xii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e s"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_484">Salisbury, Wiltshire.
                        Cathedral church of St Mary the Virgin; see removed from Sherborne in 1078.
                        </orgName><p>'Liber iste pertinet ad ecclesiam cathedralem Sar'' inside the
                        cover, s. xiv.</p><p>The same scribe s. xii wrote the letters 'D.M.' as a
                        'nota bene' sign in the margins of Aberdeen UL 216, Bodl. 392, 444 (fols.
                        1--27), 756, 765, 768, 835; Fell 1, 4; Rawl. C.723; Salisbury Cath. 10, 24,
                        25, 37, 67, 78, 88, 106, 128, 129, 135, 140, 154, 159, 165.</p><p> Salisbury
                        Cathedral 35, 36, 106, 109, 115, 118, 168, 197 contain the same marking with
                        letters 'vz' in pencil, by one hand, s. xiii (?). Cf. N. R. Ker in Wilts.
                        Archaeol. and Nat. hist. Mag. 53 (1949), p. 174.</p><p> </p><note
                        type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Young 131</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Later alienated.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sotheby sale 16 Dec. 1970 lot 25 (with facs.
                     of fol. 83v), but withdrawn before the sale and sold by the owners, Lancing
                     College, to Salisbury Cathedral for £1500.</provenance>
               </history>
